    "q-81134": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81134",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $E={40,44,48,…,140},$ which collection of subsets of $E$ is a partition of $E?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $E$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $E$ where every element of $E$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{40,44,48,…,76},{80,84,88,…,92},{96,100,104,…,140}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{40,44,48,…,72},{104,108,112,…,140}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $E$ (such as $96$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{40,44,48,…,84},{56,60,64,…,140}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $56$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{24,28,32,…,140}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $28$) that do not appear in $E.$\n\n- ${{40,44,48,52},{53,54,55,…,140}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $53$) that do not appear in $E.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81134-a",
